{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pulls/31","id":5337669093,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVvZx0M8AAAABPiZd5Q","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pull/31","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pull/31.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pull/31.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/issues/31","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pulls/31/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pulls/31/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/issues/31/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/HeptaTorch/statuses/cef47b8fc36e4afefad4b4c4e53625f8f62e0a57","number":31,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Implement native HIA retained gradients and qualify the 446-function profile","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why this change is needed\n\nThe native HIA gradient profile did not expose retained non-leaf gradients with the lifetime, accumulation, and failure-order semantics observed in the pinned PyTorch reference. This change adds the retained-gradient operations and binds the resulting 446-function native image to strict ownership, numeric, rollback, and independent observer checks.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Implement native retain/query commands 93/94. First retained gradients are independent contiguous clones; subsequent gradients accumulate out of place, preserving already-held gradient identities. Weak retain metadata, saved-object error ordering, and the supported partial-failure cases are checked explicitly.\n- Add a qualification coordinator, a fresh cold-build CI stage, retained raw-evidence export, and the 446-function observer profile. Keep the existing 355/428 profiles and all accounting algorithms and negative-control rules unchanged.\n- Preserve the original producer, independent review, resource and extension evidence. The old truncated resource archive remains recorded as an original failure; complete new root executions provide the current evidence.\n- Record PR #28's final hosted admission, including 59,251 independent checks, exact artifact members, official job metadata, and the previously failed hosted runs.\n\n## Completed local validation\n\nThe fixed source is `666230f05cc6942470006d1f184135321d8cbc26a6c6ba0bf7e3cf9857fe515b`; native ELF is `7568c0a4ec40d82d3a0b46d1e8a27499dd96e8fe3fd15433523131a196da89b5`.\n\n- Fresh root compilation and 17 inherited qualification suites passed.\n- Strict retained-gradient coverage: 12 scenarios, 3,849 frames, 38,529 assertions, 1,352 exact binary32 words plus 188 Adam positions, no raw-bit differences, and 9,087,312 rollback bytes.\n- Additive optimizer 14, resource 8, typed 2, and source checks passed. Five additional regression groups passed over 947 frames.\n- The integrated local run verified/reused the recorded 17-suite producer and actually executed all six outer runners. This is explicitly distinguished from the fresh default coordinator execution required by CI.\n- The minimal 446 observer extension passed native 3/13 checks and four positive plus 18 unchanged corruption controls. Its live-32 and frozen-35 hosted evaluations have also passed, as recorded below.\n- Two independent read-only reviews checked the coordinator, original evidence, and CI wiring; the CI review passed 139 checks.\n\nThe immutable root archive contains 1,753 original members, and the integrated run contains 2,051 original members. Archived literal patch whitespace is preserved byte-for-byte.\n\n## Completed hosted acceptance\n\nThe exact head `cef47b8fc36e4afefad4b4c4e53625f8f62e0a57` and tree `09f37b090c0773d53db2bef527017fe9f0e298bf` passed all **9 checks**. The official PR checkout `45f1800a2373a3e3d121d7efaec9206cea17b4b5` has that same tree and parents `7e7e37be38457d88f214d45f261924983dc96b56` plus the exact source head.\n\n| Hosted gate | Actual result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Native PR run 43873971659 / job 133322084171 | All 80 actual steps succeeded |\n| Native push run 43873897738 / job 133321827152 | All 80 actual steps succeeded |\n| Quick run 43873971672 / 355, 428 and 446 jobs | All 13 actual steps succeeded per profile |\n| CodeQL and three language analyses | All four checks succeeded |\n\nThe fresh default coordinator `c71d40ea111b9c80e9d0987f7cd42729cc3f47ecf5a86b7e5d4ecf0659ec0ee2` actually rebuilt/executed its 17-suite producer and six outer runners. The hosted evidence explicitly has fresh execution true and producer reuse false. Its complete raw archive has 2,053 members and its input manifest binds 2,275 checked inputs; no local reuse count was substituted.\n\nThe main reports contain 63 original root reports plus their CI manifest, with 33 complete envelopes. The main journal ZIP contains 440 original members. The three quick profiles and all main profiles retain the original live-32 and frozen-35 numeric, provenance, EOF and post-close Version checks.\n\nThe independent offline admission passed **106,570 checks with zero failures** and was independently rerun by root, producing the exact same 11,623,198-byte report:\n`bd2f2c7516dfbcdab7d3d4b65883bd9ff4c4a7bea2e91900fb039fae21e752d9`.\nThe final reader is `b8b8d96d4320440c0ac5a46e642a19dc45af346283e2511d0d2fc13c41a2790f`, with retained-evidence reader `6c9685bf7f8c4433ea0391890839efd95343e2b248a9890bda9a5ebf29e7c06e`. This offline step ran neither native code nor PyTorch.\n\nTwo preliminary reader failures remain preserved: one used a global Makefile fragment count instead of the unique retained target, and one assumed the optimizer reference's unchanged-source record was a boolean rather than its exact three-key schema. The corrected reader checks the exact recipe and exact schema; no original report, numeric comparison, Version assertion, provenance requirement or cold-execution condition was changed.\n\nOriginal main artifact SHA-256 values:\n\n- Reports, artifact 14230722118: `a30e82bab9ee7d45ae4da8fe23cc1c42a77d1e2b698c07fa2258de2d0d605b17`.\n- Journals, artifact 14230722148: `f8c3a59c2a69396fcb957e6bbfa4340be9ae62e3b7cd4338ced2132dddc4284d`.\n- Retained native evidence, artifact 14229484672: `320c9ffac94871eb72499190cc37c7f3535246921a30c8160f311aefd717d0b1`.\n\n## Whole-project status\n\nThis closes a specific native retained-gradient slice only. The pinned PyTorch v2.15.0 target remains 2,590 schemas and 688 derivative entries; full-schema parity remains 0 and all 17 whole-system gates remain open/in progress under HOLD. NativeDropout/bool/history successor work is separate and is not included in this PR.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-16T13:14:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T13:53:49Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T13:51:31Z","merged_at":"2026-11-16T13:51:31Z"